1. Personal Data
1-1. Registration & Profile Information
For purposes of this Privacy Policy, “personal data” means personally identifiable information that specifically identifies you as an individual. We collect information, including personal data, in two main ways: (1) when you provide it directly to us, and (2) when we collect it passively from your browser or device as you use the Services. This includes, but is not limited to, when you:
register for Services, contests and special events;
access Services using a third-party account;
subscribe to newsletters;
purchase a product or services through TapBlaze’s online stores;
use “tell a friend,” “email this page,” or other similar features;
request technical support or other customer service; and
otherwise through your use of the Services when your information is required for use and/or participation.
The types of information may vary depending on the type of activity you are engaged in.
Information You Provide to Us:
TapBlaze may collect, process and use information you provide to us, which may include personal data. This includes, but is not limited to:
Contact information, such as your name, email address, phone number;
Identifiers from your accounts with third-party services that you use to log into the Services such as Apple and/or Facebook;
TapBlaze Services identifier (TapBlaze ID);
Registration information, including a username, password;
If you purchase physical goods from us, purchase information, such as quantity and type of goods purchased, name of purchaser, and shipping address;
Credit card payment information for your purchase, which is securely processed by our third-party payment processor;
Correspondence between you and us and records of such correspondence, such as the contents of emails you send us, support inquiries, or other feedback you provide directly to us;
Information you provide in product reviews and surveys.
1-2. TAPBLAZE ID
Some games allow players to restore their progress by using their email to register for a TapBlaze ID. TapBlaze only permits the creation of a TapBlaze ID in games with age gates when the user has identified as 16 years of age or older. We use your email address ONLY for retrieving your game progress and for no other purpose. In addition, all email addresses are hashed. If you no longer want to have your email associated with a TapBlaze ID for game progress saving, please contact us
here
and your progress and email will be deleted within 72 hours. Please mention "TAPBLAZE ID Deletion" in your email subject.
We keep data collected for the TapBlaze ID until the user’s de-registration from the Services or inactivity of 2 years.
1-3. Use of Your Information and Legal Grounds
TapBlaze may use your information for purposes of analyzing usage of the Services, providing customer and technical support, managing and providing Services (including managing advertisement serving) and to further develop the Services and other products. TapBlaze may combine non-personal data with personal data.
TapBlaze also may use your personal data to send messages to you with informative and/or commercial content about TapBlaze’s services or third party products and services TapBlaze thinks may be of interest to you, such as push notifications and newsletters for the players with TapBlaze ID who are 16 years of age or over, that could involve third party services.
We use your information for the following purposes and based on the following legal grounds:
To enter into and execute an agreement with you as set forth in our
Terms and Conditions
:
- For account registration purposes; and
- To provide and operate the Services.

For the purposes of our legitimate business interests:
- To respond to your requests, complaints and communications, to verify your identity, to process your transactions, to provide technical support and troubleshooting, and for other customer service purposes, including to facilitate account recovery and process account deletion requests;
- To send non-marketing communications such as technical issues or bug fixes;
- To develop new products and services including, but not limited to, in-game events, production of merchandise;
- For player identification, fraud prevention, and detection of improper usage;
- Notification of activities to friends, user search;
- To tailor the content and information that we may send or display to you, to offer personalized content and to assist us in advertising our services;
- To send you event information, marketing messages and advertisements;
- For auditing purposes, including counting online ad impressions and verifying positioning and quality of ad impressions;
- To better understand how users access and use our Services, to respond to user desires and preferences, and for other research and analytical purposes;
- To administer our contests; and
- To determine, exercise or defend our legal position and rights.
To comply with our legal obligations:
- Where required by law or legal process; and
- To comply with a binding request.

2. Non-Personal Data
For purposes of this Privacy Policy, “non-personal data” means information that does not directly identify you. Additionally, non-personal data means “aggregate” and “de-personalized” information, which is data TapBlaze collects about your use of TapBlaze Services, from which any personally identifiable data has been removed.
TapBlaze may use tools or third-party analytical software to automatically collect and use certain non-personal data that does not directly enable TapBlaze to identify you. The types of non-personal data TapBlaze may collect and use include, but are not limited to:
(i) device properties (model, service provider information, OS information, language and country information);
(ii) device software platform and firmware;
(iii) mobile phone carrier;
(iv) general/coarse location data;
(v) game activity and achievements (scores, credits, access logs);
(vi) improper usage record and fraud detection information;
(vii) birthdate, gender;
(viii) friend connections; and
(ix) marketing preferences, such as records of your requests to opt out of marketing communications.
TapBlaze may use and disclose to TapBlaze’s partners and contractors the collected non-personal data for purposes of analyzing usage of the Services, serving advertisements, managing and providing the Services and to further develop the Services.
If any of the non-personal data listed above is combined with personal data (such as a name, email or other online identifier) or reidentified in a way that permits us to identify you individually, we will treat it as personal data.

